{"path":"io/c/fgetc","title":"std::fgetc, std::getc","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>fgetc, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>getc","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/c/fgetc","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"Reads the next character from the given input stream.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/cstdio\">&lt;cstdio&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> fgetc<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/FILE\"><span class=\"kw1892\">std::<span class=\"me2\">FILE</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> stream <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> getc<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/FILE\"><span class=\"kw1892\">std::<span class=\"me2\">FILE</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> stream <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Reads the next character from the given input stream.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> stream\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> to read the character from\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>The obtained character on success or <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c\">EOF</a></span> on failure.\n</p><p>If the failure has been caused by end of file condition, additionally sets the <i>eof</i> indicator (see <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/feof\">std::feof()</a></span>) on <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">stream</span></code>. If the failure has been caused by some other error, sets the <i>error</i> indicator (see <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/ferror\">std::ferror()</a></span>) on <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">stream</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstdio&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstdlib&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> is_ok <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/program/EXIT_status\"><span class=\"kw977\">EXIT_FAILURE</span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    FILE<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> fp <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/fopen\"><span class=\"kw1830\">std::<span class=\"me2\">fopen</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"/tmp/test.txt\"</span>, <span class=\"st0\">\"w+\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">!</span>fp<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/perror\"><span class=\"kw1888\">std::<span class=\"me2\">perror</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"File opening failed\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> is_ok<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> c<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// Note: int, not char, required to handle EOF</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">while</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>c <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">fgetc</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>fp<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c\"><span class=\"kw1897\">EOF</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"co1\">// Standard C I/O file reading loop</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/putchar\"><span class=\"kw1844\">std::<span class=\"me2\">putchar</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>c<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/ferror\"><span class=\"kw1887\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ferror</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>fp<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/puts\"><span class=\"kw1845\">std::<span class=\"me2\">puts</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"I/O error when reading\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">else</span> <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/feof\"><span class=\"kw1886\">std::<span class=\"me2\">feof</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>fp<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/puts\"><span class=\"kw1845\">std::<span class=\"me2\">puts</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"End of file reached successfully\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        is_ok <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/program/EXIT_status\"><span class=\"kw976\">EXIT_SUCCESS</span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/fclose\"><span class=\"kw1833\">std::<span class=\"me2\">fclose</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>fp<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> is_ok<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>End of file reached successfully</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/gets\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>gets</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-deprecated-cxx11\">(deprecated in C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx14\">(removed in C++14)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  reads a character string from <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/std_streams\">stdin</a></span> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/fputc\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>fputc</span><span>putc</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  writes a character to a file stream <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/ungetc\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>ungetc</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  puts a character back into a file stream <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/io/fgetc\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>fgetc</span>, <span>getc</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/c","title":"C-style file input/output"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::fgetc, std::getc","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Reads the next character from the given input stream."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"stream"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The obtained character on success or EOF on failure."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"gets","note":"reads a character string from stdin"},{"label":"fputc, putc","note":"writes a character to a file stream"},{"label":"ungetc","note":"puts a character back into a file stream"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++14"],"wordCount":197,"codeBlockCount":2}
